Volume = {41},
Number = {3},
Pages = {138-150},
Month = {JUN},
Abstract = {In the public perception air pollution is a priority issue only in urban
   and industrialized areas, whereas climate change is recognized as a
   global problem. However, air pollution is largely driven by the some
   emissions as climate change (i.e. traffic, energy sector, agriculture:
   e.g., carbon dioxide, methane, carbon monoxide, hydrocarbons, sulfur
   dioxide and nitrogen oxides emissions). Emission control for environment
   and climate protection thus requires to reduce emissions from the some
   sources. In addition, weather and climate affects the cycling of
   atmospheric trace substances and the emissions of trace species from
   biogenic sources as for instance the marine biosphere or vegetation.
   Climate is changing, and will continue to change. As climate changes,
   urban and regional air quality will change as well. Development of
   strategies for protection of climate and environment requires better
   integration of the scientific communities dealing with climate and
   air-quality issues.},
